module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.string_interpolation_read_as_literal_text_by_v2

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data string_interpolation_read_as_literal_text_by_v2: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "string_interpolation_read_as_literal_text_by_v2" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**FOUND: a string literal that interpolates a name in v1 was read by v2 as the literal bytes of that name** (INVALID STATE: `\"\{repository_path}\"` in a .dag source. The seed tokenizer (v1.compiler.tokenize scan_string_body) ends the string body at the interpolation start and reads `repository_path` as a reference. Until XL-2, the v2 lexer's string rule (v2.extdeps.languages.dag dag_string_literal_lex_rule, body dag_string_body_element_pattern) had no interpolation arm, so the same source was one string literal whose text contained the braces. HARM: one spelling, two meanings across the two compilers, the meaning fork of DESIGN section 3. DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the escape `\\{` is a literal brace in both compilers, so only an unescaped brace differed.)",

    "CLIMBED (XL-2, gunbc#13693): dag_string_body_element_pattern now admits no hole opener, disjointly from dag_string_hole_opener_pattern (the same starts v1.compiler.tokenize should_start_interpolation uses: IdentStartChar, `(`, `!`, `-`). A hole-free spelling is dag_token_string_literal; a hole is dag_token_string_template_head plus the hole's ordinary tokens. The grammar reads ^dag_string_template; body_lower_string_template rewrites it to concat. The body pattern HAS an interpolation split — the sentence that it has none is the pre-climb state, not the current one.",

    "RESIDUAL FORK, review 78485 on gunbc#13693: the eight single-character escapes were admitted as a sequence, but the unicode-scalar form (backslash, u, brace, hex, brace) was not. In a letter-hex spelling the backslash and u lexed as StringTextChar and the brace plus letter matched the hole opener (the letter is IdentStartChar), so a documented Unicode escape was a template hole. A digit-hex spelling survived only because a digit is not a hole start. That is a meaning fork against this module's own escape table (DESIGN sections 3 and 5). CLIMBED on the same PR: dag_string_unicode_escape_prefix_pattern consumes the backslash-u-brace prefix the way v1 scan_string_body does, so a unicode-escape brace is never a hole opener. Discriminating red: v2.test.tokenize.string_literal_raw_newline unicode_escape_letter_hex_lexes_as_one_string_literal. Positive control: unicode_escape_digit_hex_lexes_as_one_string_literal.",

    "SPECIMEN, found 2026-10-02 grounding XL-2 PR3a (service realization). Grep sizing over dag/ and src/v2 at authoring time, not an oracle: 758 string literals in 87 files carry an unescaped `\{name}`, 633 of them on service transport lines.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT (original class): below the floor -- silent. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. The interpolation split and the unicode-escape prefix are both lex-decidable. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER for any remaining escape/hole fork: a documented numeric escape that still opens a hole, or a hole opener that v1 opens and v2 does not.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a v2 string token stream disagrees with v1 scan_string_body on whether a brace starts interpolation, including a brace that v1 consumed as the `\u{` escape prefix.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.extdeps.languages.dag", decl_name: "dag_string_unicode_escape_prefix_pattern", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.extdeps.languages.dag", decl_name: "dag_string_body_element_pattern", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.tokenize.string_literal_raw_newline", decl_name: "unicode_escape_letter_hex_lexes_as_one_string_literal", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.tokenize.string_literal_raw_newline", decl_name: "unicode_escape_digit_hex_lexes_as_one_string_literal", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
